description:
As discussed in MR: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/25797

This patch is to fix the display of calculated PSN fields for various PDS headers, The wire-level offset fields (ack_psn_offset, sack_psn_offset, clear_psn_offset) are now dissected at their correct byte positions in the packet to keep alignment with the UET specification.

The resulting computed PSN values are marked as generated fields (in brackets []).

* The `Start_PSN` example:

![start_psn_display_example](/uploads/a6d4b59dafc04ea911ccb8c938cbfb3d/start_psn_display_example.png){width=378 height=43}

* Before the patch: 

![before_sack_psn](/uploads/320a331351dd77e18cc977a2139746cc/before_sack_psn.png){width=295 height=23}

* With the patch:

![patched_sack_psn](/uploads/0e0b608c815f3665f454e60b06ada0a2/patched_sack_psn.png){width=378 height=43}

* The pcap used for this patch contains PDS_RUD_Request, PDS_ACK, and PDS_ACK_CC: [uether_psn_calculation.pcap](/uploads/a60ba02d28edc09d066db52565a127c0/uether_psn_calculation.pcap)

